    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Greek kingdom on both shores of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kerch-strait">Kerch Strait</a>, ruled from Panticapaeum (modern Kerch) by the Spartocid dynasty for over three centuries.</li><li>Its grain exports helped feed classical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#athens">Athens</a>, which honoured its kings with citizenship, privileges and crowns.</li><li>It passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a> and then lived on as a Roman client kingdom until the Hunnic invasions.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Jewish communities in Panticapaeum freed slaves in the synagogue and recorded it on stone; one such manumission inscription dates from 81 CE.</p></aside>
    </section>

